{"family": "unidepth_v2", "task": "depth", "name": "UniDepth V2", "plain": "UniDepth V2: metric depth from one image without known camera data. Non-commercial licence.", "summary": "UniDepth V2 (Piccinelli et al. 2025): universal metric depth from a DINOv2 ViT-L encoder and a camera-prompted decoder; predicts depth, 3-D points, a confidence map and the pinhole intrinsics, or uses given intrinsics.", "tier": "stable", "upstream": "https://github.com/lpiccinelli-eth/UniDepth", "upstream_commit": "8d8cfe4", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "UniDepthV2: Universal Monocular Metric Depth Estimation Made Simpler", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.20110", "date": "2025-02-27", "venue": "arXiv", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["fastbb", "cudnn_hacc", "dpt_fused"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "confidence", "default": true, "bounds": "", "effect": "output"}], "outputs": [{"name": "depth", "extra": false}, {"name": "points", "extra": false}, {"name": "intrinsics", "extra": false}, {"name": "confidence", "extra": false}], "output_info": {"kind": "metric"}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": ["The confidence head adds measurable time; the option confidence = false skips it."], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: a depth or inverse-depth map. `kind` (a card field, `result.kind`) says what the numbers mean: `metric` = metres; `scale_invariant`, `affine_invariant` and `affine_invariant_inverse` are relative (unknown scale or shift, not metres). Metric models that use the focal length take `model(image, intrinsics=K)` (K `[3, 3]`, pixels of the input): `metric3d-vit-large` and `da3metric-large` need it for correct metres (`da3metric-large`: metres = output x focal / 300; without `intrinsics=` a 300 px focal length is assumed, wrong for a real camera). `unidepth-v